---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-slu-intentions/20261107-01/';
type Row = { reported_2024_choice: string; raw_prior_base: number;
	kish_weight_concentration_base: number; intended_house_pct: Record<string, number> };
const review: { rows: Row[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}intentions.json`, 'utf8'));
const pct = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(1)}%`;
---

<section id="participation-house-intentions" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="house-intentions-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Earlier independent evidence · August intentions only</p>
		<h2 id="house-intentions-title">Missouri: prior choice and intended House vote</h2>
		<p>The SLU / YouGov poll interviewed 900 registered likely voters on August 13–24, 2026.
			This table is <strong>not observed November switching or turnout</strong>. It records
			intended House-party choice in each respondent's own district, not a statewide House race
			or a named-candidate district result.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Missouri August intended House choice by reported 2024 vote">
		<table>
			<caption>Weighted intentions among likely voters reporting each prior presidential choice.
				All other and unsure responses remain in the denominator. These are not percentages
				of the original 2024 coalitions.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Reported 2024 choice</th><th scope="col">Raw prior n</th>
				<th scope="col">Kish diagnostic</th><th scope="col">Intended D</th>
				<th scope="col">Intended R</th><th scope="col">Other</th><th scope="col">Not sure</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{review.rows.map(row => <tr data-slu-prior={row.reported_2024_choice}>
				<th scope="row">{row.reported_2024_choice}</th>
				<td data-slu-base>{row.raw_prior_base}</td>
				<td data-slu-kish>{row.kish_weight_concentration_base.toFixed(1)}</td>
				{['D', 'R', 'Other', 'Not sure'].map(party =>
					<td data-slu-choice={party}>{pct(row.intended_house_pct[party])}</td>)}
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><strong>No drop-off estimate from this sample.</strong> Everyone was screened as almost
		certain or probable to vote. The sample does not observe an eligible nonvoter comparison
		group or completed November participation. We do not multiply these August intentions by
		November ballot totals, infer mass switchers, or allocate district, county or precinct estimates.</p>
	<p>Raw n and the Kish weight-concentration diagnostic are not design-aware conditional precision.
		No subgroup confidence intervals are supplied; one-decimal display is not a precision guarantee.
		Sampling, selection, recall and intention error remain. This separate earlier study does not
		fill Missouri's missing post-election SSRS state table.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Methods, source versions and complete selected inputs</summary>
		<p><a href="https://www.slu.edu/research/research-institute/big-ideas/slu-poll/-pdf/slu-poll-august-2026-topline-results.pdf">The wave-specific questionnaire and methods</a>
			describe weighting 1,074 registered voters, including 2024 presidential-choice calibration,
			before selecting 900 likely voters and trimming/recentering their weights. That does not
			establish that the selected likely voters were forced to match the 2024 electorate.
			No new historical reweighting is applied here.</p>
		<p>The complete selected aggregate archive contains both broad prior groups and all four
			weighted House responses, source URLs and hashes, qualification, exact code and tests.
			Raw joint-cell counts, fine demographic cells, respondent records and copyrighted native
			PDF/HTML documents are not mirrored. Offline reproduction starts from the complete selected
			aggregates; re-running the original record aggregation separately requires obtaining
			the pinned publicly offered native data from SLU. Analysis is not endorsed by SLU or YouGov.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete Missouri intention aggregates + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}intentions.json`} download>Missouri intentions + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Missouri archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-house-intentions { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
